E["npc:brann-bronzebeard"] = {t="npc",n="Brann Bronzebeard",z="silithus",s="In southern Silithus, Brann Bronzebeard's companions wait for word from his latest expedition. The youngest brother of King Magni and Muradin is famed across Azeroth as an explorer, archaeologist, and founding leader of the explorers' league. His search for titan ruins and ancient history has led him deep into the deadly wastes.",h="In southern Silithus, Brann Bronzebeard's companions wait for word from his latest expedition.",sec={{t="A Royal Wanderer",b="Brann Bronzebeard chose the open wilds while his eldest brother Magni ruled Ironforge and Muradin served on the front lines. A veteran of the Second War, Brann turned his strength toward the forgotten past when peace came. As a leader of the explorers' league, he charted the Eastern Kingdoms, from Elwynn Forest to the jungles of Zul'Gurub. Then he crossed the Great Sea to seek the mysteries of ancient Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in Silithus",b="Reports from the Cenarion Circle spoke of the Old God C'Thun and the slumbering qiraji swarm. They drew Brann south to Silithus, where he founded Bronzebeard Encampment with Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge.\n\nThe priestess Natalia Mar'alith had gone mad from horrors whispering in the shifting sands. She raided their camp and demanded Brann lead them back into Hive'Regal. Brann refused, and she attacked. He, his crew, and his pet ape Glibb barely fought her off.",sp=1},{t="Beyond the Scarab Wall",b="Brann Bronzebeard set his sights on the sealed kingdom behind the Scarab Wall. He found a hidden tunnel beneath the ancient barrier and entered alone. Before leaving, he gave Glibb to the expedition with strict written orders: plenty of food, water, and affectionate hugs.\n\nRutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge remain in southern Silithus. They wait for word from Brann within the silithid hives.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Brann Bronzebeard?",a="Brann Bronzebeard is the youngest brother of King Magni Bronzebeard of Ironforge and a co-founder and driving force of the dwarven explorers' league. A renowned archaeologist and cartographer, he travels Azeroth's most dangerous frontiers in search of titan artifacts and lost civilizations.",al={"who is brann","brann lore","brann bronzebeard backstory"}},{q="Where is Brann Bronzebeard right now?",a="Brann Bronzebeard's trail leads to Silithus, where Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge keep Bronzebeard Encampment. They may know about his latest expedition.",al={"brann location","where to find brann","where is brann in silithus"}},{q="What happened to his camp in Silithus?",a="Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge have troubling news about Brann Bronzebeard's expedition. Speak with them to learn what happened at the camp.",al={"what happened at bronzebeard encampment","who attacked brann's camp","natalia attack brann"}},{q="Who is Glibb?",a="Glibb is Brann Bronzebeard's companion ape. He is staying with the explorers at Bronzebeard Encampment in Silithus.",al={"glibb ape","brann's monkey","brann pet"}},{q="Did Brann fight in the Second War?",a="Yes. Brann Bronzebeard is a veteran of the Second War. In peacetime, he turned his strength toward uncovering the forgotten past.",al={"brann second war","was brann in the alliance army","brann and muradin war"}},{q="Why is Brann interested in Silithus?",a="Reports from the Cenarion Circle about the Old God C'Thun and the slumbering qiraji swarm drew Brann Bronzebeard to Silithus. His interest in titan history led him to seek a way beyond the sealed Scarab Wall and inspect the ruins firsthand.",al={"why did brann go to silithus","brann silithus purpose","brann c'thun"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Brann Bronzebeard's passion for uncovering the roots of his people's titan heritage. He is the youngest brother of King Magni.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you benefit from the knowledge and archives Brann Bronzebeard's expeditions build. His habit of vanishing without a trace often frustrates Ironforge's leadership."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","brann","bronzebeard","explorers league","frankal","glibb","natalia mar'alith","rutgar","scarab wall","silithus"},rel={"subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","subzone:scarab-wall","npc:rutgar-glyphshaper","npc:natalia-mar-alith","subzone:hive-regal","topic:explorers-league","zone:silithus","zone:ironforge"},src={"Brann Bronzebeard"}}
E["npc:commander-mar-alith"] = {t="npc",n="Commander Mar'alith",z="silithus",s="At Cenarion Hold, Commander Mar'alith holds the line against the dangers of Silithus. He leads the fight against silithid swarms and Twilight's Hammer cultists, while grief over his missing wife weighs on him.",h="At Cenarion Hold, Commander Mar'alith holds the line against the dangers of Silithus.",sec={{t="Commander of the Hold",b="At Cenarion Hold, Commander Mar'alith guards the Cenarion Circle's desert stronghold. The druids study Silithus's ancient ecological and cosmic anomalies, while he directs the work of war. His forces strike at the silithid hives of Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal. They keep the incursions from overwhelming the expedition's central foothold.",sp=0},{t="Grief in the Desert",b="Commander Mar'alith's stern bearing cannot hide his grief. His beloved wife, Natalia Mar'alith, went into the shifting sands on an assignment for the Circle and did not return. He holds to his duty to the Cenarion expedition, though he longs for news of what happened to her in the wastes.",sp=0},{t="A Tragic Fate",b="Natalia Mar'alith succumbed to madness amid the desert's whispers. Then a Qiraji crystal brainwashed her into serving C'Thun. The truth leaves Commander Mar'alith deeply shaken. Even through heartbreak, he directs Silithus's defense against the horrors below.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Commander Mar'alith?",a="Commander Mar'alith commands the Cenarion Circle's military forces at Cenarion Hold. He organizes scouts, defenses, and strikes against the silithid hives across Silithus.",al={"maralith","who is commander maralith","night elf commander silithus"}},{q="Where can Commander Mar'alith be found?",a="Commander Mar'alith can be found inside Cenarion Hold, the Cenarion Circle's main neutral settlement in the sands of Silithus.",al={"maralith location","where is maralith"}},{q="What happened to his wife, Natalia?",a="Natalia Mar'alith vanished into the desert during an expedition and never returned. Following her trail through Silithus reveals what became of her.",al={"where is natalia","dearest natalia","natalia maralith fate"},sp=1},{q="Why does Mar'alith seem absent-minded?",a="Sorrow and anxiety over his missing wife and her fate weigh on Commander Mar'alith. Even so, he directs the fortress's defense.",al={"why is maralith distracted","maralith acting weird"}},{q="What tasks does Commander Mar'alith assign to adventurers?",a="Commander Mar'alith sends champions against silithids in Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal. He also sets them against the Twilight's Hammer and asks them to investigate his wife's fate.",al={"maralith quests","what quests does maralith give"}},{q="Is Commander Mar'alith a druid?",a="No. Commander Mar'alith is an armored sentinel and warrior commander. He directs the expedition's military defense and tactics rather than wielding druidic magic.",al={"is maralith a druid","maralith class"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share the sentinels' and warriors' devotion to guarding Kalimdor beside the druids, even at great personal cost.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the work of battlefield command. Mar'alith directs the fighting in heavy armor and bears a massive glaive among the settlement's mystics and nature keepers."},kw={"cenarion circle","cenarion hold","commander mar'alith","hive'ashi","hive'regal","hive'zora","mar'alith","natalia mar'alith","silithus"},rel={"subzone:cenarion-hold","npc:natalia-mar-alith","zone:silithus","topic:cenarion-circle","subzone:hive-ashi","subzone:hive-zora","subzone:hive-regal","topic:night-elf"},src={"Commander Mar'alith"}}
E["npc:highlord-demitrian"] = {t="npc",n="Highlord Demitrian",z="silithus",s="Among the strange crystals of northwestern Silithus, Highlord Demitrian waits alone. He calls himself a loyal servant of Prince Thunderaan and knows how to wake the sleeping elemental lord. Those who bring him ancient elemental bindings seek the Windseeker's power.",h="Among the strange crystals of northwestern Silithus, Highlord Demitrian waits alone.",sec={{t="Hermit of the Crystal Vale",b="In the Crystal Vale, Demitrian lingers at an abandoned encampment in Silithus's desolate wastes. The ruined camp belongs to the Twilight's Hammer, and the solitary human seems out of place there. Yet Demitrian's chief purpose is to herald Prince Thunderaan, the Windseeker. He gives visitors little notice unless they carry proof of the Windseeker's shattered essence.",sp=0},{t="The Vessel of Rebirth",b="Demitrian's purpose is to bring about Thunderaan's resurrection. When someone brings him the Bindings of the Windseeker, relics torn from fire elementals within the Molten Core, he gives them the Vessel of Rebirth. To restore his prince's physical form, he demands rare elemental reagents. They include vast quantities of enchanted elementium and the essence of the Firelord.",sp=1},{t="Betrayal of the Windseeker",b="Demitrian's ritual calls Prince Thunderaan into the Crystal Vale, where the restored Windseeker must be faced in battle. Once the elemental lord is vanquished, the Dormant Wind Kissed Blade is recovered and brought to the terrified Demitrian. In exchange, he awakens Thunderfury.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Highlord Demitrian?",a="Find Demitrian at the Ravaged Twilight Camp in the Crystal Vale, at Silithus's far northwestern corner.",al={"demitrian location","where is demitrian","demitrian silithus spot"}},{q="Why does Demitrian only give a generic response?",a="Demitrian gives no further response unless you carry at least one half of the Bindings of the Windseeker. Baron Geddon and Garr hold these rare treasures within the Molten Core.",al={"demitrian won't talk to me","how to get demitrian quest","demitrian gossip"}},{q="What is Demitrian's relationship to Prince Thunderaan?",a="Demitrian is the sworn mortal servant of Prince Thunderaan. He seeks the prince's severed bindings to restore the elemental lord to the physical plane.",al={"who does demitrian serve","demitrian thunderaan connection","is demitrian twilight hammer"}},{q="What happens when you bring him all the materials for the vessel?",a="Demitrian performs a ritual that calls Prince Thunderaan into the Crystal Vale and restores the Windseeker to the physical plane.",al={"summoning thunderaan","what does demitrian do with the vessel","crystal vale summon"},sp=1},{q="Is Demitrian affiliated with the Twilight's Hammer cult?",a="Demitrian is tied to the Twilight's Hammer and dwells in their ravaged camp. He speaks of the Old Gods with reverence, yet his sworn devotion is to Prince Thunderaan.",al={"is demitrian a cultist","demitrian twilight camp","demitrian faction"}},{q="How do you get Thunderfury from him?",a="Bring Demitrian both halves of the Bindings of the Windseeker, taken from Baron Geddon and Garr in the Molten Core. Then gather the rare materials he demands for the Vessel of Rebirth. The ritual's outcome and the blade's awakening are told in the hidden passages.",al={"how to get thunderfury","thunderfury quest finish","demitrian blade"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Thunderaan's rebirth calls for extensive blacksmithing skill to forge Enchanted Elementium Bars from raw ore and fiery essences.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior seeking Thunderfury, seek Demitrian to begin the trial of unbinding and awakening the Windseeker.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue hunting the Windseeker's legendary blade, bargain with Demitrian in Silithus to restore the shattered prince."},kw={"crystal vale","demitrian","highlord demitrian","silithus","thunderaan","thunderfury","vessel of rebirth","windseeker"},rel={"npc:thunderaan","subzone:crystal-vale","zone:silithus","subzone:ravaged-twilight-camp","topic:elemental-plane","topic:skywall"},src={"Highlord Demitrian"}}
E["npc:natalia-mar-alith"] = {t="npc",n="Natalia Mar'alith",z="silithus",s="Deep in Hive'Regal, Natalia Mar'alith has vanished among the silithid. The night elf priestess and Cenarion Circle researcher entered the wastes of Silithus with her husband, Commander Mar'alith, then went on an expedition into the hives.",h="Deep in Hive'Regal, Natalia Mar'alith has vanished among the silithid.",sec={{t="A Tragic Descent",b="At Cenarion Hold, the Cenarion Circle watches the awakening sands. Natalia joined her husband, Commander Mar'alith, in the wastes, hoping to learn why the silithid were returning and what lay among the ancient Qiraji ruins. She then joined an expedition led by Brann Bronzebeard, the famed explorer, with the dwarven researchers Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge.",sp=0},{t="The Crystal of Hive'Regal",b="The expedition followed strange emanations into the southern reaches of Hive'Regal. Deep in its heart, the companions found a colossal crystal marked with ancient Qiraji glyphs. Natalia leaned close to study the markings, drawn by the crystal's whispering resonance. Dark magic overwhelmed her mind and bound her will to C'Thun.\n\nHer dwarven companions carried Natalia to Cenarion Hold, where druids woke her. Weeks later, she stormed back into their camp, possessed and demanding to return to the hive. They had to fight her off. Now Natalia guards the hive's dread master with zeal.",sp=1},{t="The Commander's Anguish",b="At Cenarion Hold, Commander Mar'alith clings to hope that his wife can be saved. He cannot accept that her mind has been irrevocably shattered. Those who brave Hive'Regal find no captive awaiting rescue. Natalia is a ruthless servant of madness, wielding sacred priest magic warped by the Old God's malice.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Natalia Mar'alith?",a="Natalia Mar'alith is a night elf priestess of the Cenarion Circle and Commander Mar'alith's wife. She joined Brann Bronzebeard's expedition into Hive'Regal to study the silithid's resurgence, where dark ancient magic overcame her.",al={"natalia maralith","who is natalia","commander maraliths wife"},sp=1},{q="Where can I find Natalia Mar'alith?",a="Natalia Mar'alith is deep in Hive'Regal's tunnels in southern Silithus, keeping watch before a glowing crystal covered in glyphs.",al={"natalia location","where is natalia","hive regal priestess"}},{q="Why is Natalia hostile to adventurers?",a="As Natalia studied a Qiraji crystal, the whispers of the Old God C'Thun corrupted her and shattered her mind. She now fiercely defends the crystal from anyone who enters the hive.",al={"why did natalia attack me","why is natalia crazy","natalia brainwashed"},sp=1},{q="Who was with Natalia when she went missing?",a="Natalia entered Hive'Regal with Brann Bronzebeard, Rutgar Glyphshaper, and Frankal Stonebridge. Rutgar and Frankal survived and retreated to the Bronzebeard Encampment in southern Silithus to tell what happened.",al={"natalia expedition","who was with natalia","brann and natalia"}},{q="Why is she so dangerous in combat?",a="Natalia keeps her formidable priest powers. Her Psychic Scream scatters attackers, and her Greater Heals restore her strength at almost no cost, making her difficult to defeat without constant interruptions.",al={"natalia fight","how to beat natalia","natalia heal"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Natalia's fall reminds the kaldorei that even their most dedicated priestesses can fall prey to the ancient horrors beneath Silithus's sands.",["faction:Alliance"]="At the Bronzebeard Encampment, Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge share grim details of Natalia's fall with Alliance explorers retracing Brann's expedition."},kw={"brann bronzebeard","cenarion hold","hive'regal","into the maw of madness","mar'alith","maralith","natalia","silithus"},rel={"npc:commander-mar-alith","subzone:hive-regal","zone:silithus","subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","npc:brann-bronzebeard","npc:rutgar-glyphshaper","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:old-god"},src={"Natalia Mar'alith"}}
E["npc:rutgar-glyphshaper"] = {t="npc",n="Rutgar Glyphshaper",z="silithus",s="At the Bronzebeard Encampment, Rutgar Glyphshaper studies the silithid hives. The dwarven archaeologist came to Silithus with Brann Bronzebeard’s expedition to uncover the hives’ mysteries in their ancient relics and runes. Brann has wandered into the desert, but Rutgar carries on.",h="At the Bronzebeard Encampment, Rutgar Glyphshaper studies the silithid hives.",sec={{t="The Bronzebeard Expedition",b="Rutgar Glyphshaper came to Silithus with Brann Bronzebeard to explore the vast silithid hives and recover relics buried beneath the desert. Their expedition made camp at the Bronzebeard Encampment, south of Cenarion Hold. Rutgar and his companions often entered the hives for inscribed stones and runic artifacts. At times, Cenarion night elf researchers worked alongside them.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Hives",b="In Hive'Regal, Rutgar and the night elf priestess Natalia Mar'alith found a strange glyphed crystal. Its influence left Natalia in a trance, so the dwarves carried her to Cenarion Hold for healing. Later, she returned to their camp in a wild frenzy and demanded to go back to the hive. Rutgar and the expedition fought her off, and Natalia fled into the dunes.",sp=1},{t="Deciphering the Silithid",b="Brann Bronzebeard has disappeared into the wastes, as he often does. Rutgar remains at camp, gathering crystalline rubbings and working to decipher the insectoid glyphs scattered through the hives. He hopes to piece together the silithid’s history and trace where Brann has gone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Rutgar Glyphshaper?",a="Rutgar Glyphshaper is a scholar and explorer with Brann Bronzebeard’s archaeological expedition in Silithus. He is based at the Bronzebeard Encampment.",al={"rutgar","who is rutgar","rutgar glyphshaper info"}},{q="Where is Brann Bronzebeard?",a="Brann Bronzebeard wandered alone into the wastes of Silithus on one of his usual scouting trips. Rutgar and the rest of the crew remain at the encampment to study the hives.",al={"where is brann","where did brann go","brann missing"}},{q="What happened to Natalia Mar'alith at the camp?",a="After an ancient crystal in Hive'Regal influenced her, Natalia Mar'alith returned to the Bronzebeard Encampment in a violent rage. She attacked Rutgar, Brann, and the crew, then vanished into the desert.",al={"what happened to natalia","natalia attack","priestess attacked camp"},sp=1},{q="Why is Rutgar studying the silithid crystals?",a="Rutgar studies the silithid crystals to translate the ancient glyphs carved into them. He hopes to learn the silithid's origins and find clues to Brann's whereabouts.",al={"why glyphs","what is rutgar studying","glyphed crystals"}},{q="Has Ironforge sent aid to the expedition?",a="No. The expedition asked Ironforge for military support, but the dwarven kingdom declined, saying its forces were already stretched too thin defending the realm.",al={"ironforge reinforcements","ironforge army silithus"}},{q="Where is the Bronzebeard Encampment located?",a="The Bronzebeard Encampment lies in southern Silithus, south of Cenarion Hold and just west of Hive'Regal.",al={"where is bronzebeard encampment","encampment location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize Rutgar’s stubborn devotion to the Explorer’s League. He risks life and limb deep in hostile insect hives for ancient knowledge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can find friendly faces at a rare outpost in the harsh southern desert. Rutgar’s crew has no official backing from the Ironforge crown."},kw={"brann","bronzebeard","crystal","glyphs","glyphshaper","maralith","regal","rutgar","silithus"},rel={"subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","npc:brann-bronzebeard","subzone:hive-regal","subzone:cenarion-hold","zone:silithus","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Rutgar Glyphshaper"}}
E["npc:thunderaan"] = {t="npc",n="Thunderaan",z="silithus",s="In Silithus, Thunderaan's scattered bindings may open the way to his return. Ragnaros struck down the Prince of Air and sealed away the essence he could not consume. Highlord Demitrian waits for those who recover both halves.",h="In Silithus, Thunderaan's scattered bindings may open the way to his return.",sec={{t="The Elemental Sundering",b="During the Elemental Sundering, fire and air warred deep within Azeroth for five thousand years. Ragnaros sought Thunderaan's destruction and power. Baron Geddon and Garr, his lieutenants, ambushed and betrayed the Prince. Then Ragnaros struck him down with Sulfuras, the Firelord's hammer. Thunderaan's essence was too mighty for Ragnaros to consume in full.",sp=0},{t="The Shattered Talisman",b="Ragnaros could not devour all of the Prince of Air's essence. He sealed what remained in a talisman of elemental binding, then shattered it into two flawless halves so Thunderaan could not reform. Baron Geddon received one half and Garr the other. Both were hidden in the volcanic depths of the Molten Core beneath Blackrock Mountain.",sp=0},{t="Rebirth in Silithus",b="Highlord Demitrian, an eccentric hermit allied with the Twilight's Hammer in Silithus's arid dunes, performs a ritual when both binding fragments are brought to him. The ritual manifests Thunderaan, the Prince of Air, and his fury brings the summoners to battle. His legendary blade is Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thunderaan?",a="Thunderaan is the Prince of Air, a noble and devastating elemental lord aligned with the wind. Ragnaros overwhelmed him long ago and sealed away the essence that remained.",al={"who is prince thunderaan","prince of air","thunderaan lore"}},{q="How was Thunderaan defeated originally?",a="During the Elemental Sundering, Baron Geddon and Garr betrayed Thunderaan alongside Ragnaros. Ragnaros crushed the Prince with Sulfuras and consumed part of his essence, but could not digest it all. He sealed the remainder in a talisman split in two.",al={"how did thunderaan die","ragnaros vs thunderaan","elemental sundering"}},{q="Where are the pieces of his binding held?",a="Garr and Baron Geddon hold the two flawless halves of Thunderaan's binding deep inside the Molten Core beneath Blackrock Mountain.",al={"where are bindings of the windseeker","bindings of thunderaan location","garr and geddon bindings"}},{q="Why is Highlord Demitrian in Silithus involved?",a="Highlord Demitrian, allied with the Twilight's Hammer in Silithus, knows the arts needed to reconstitute the shattered talisman and summon the Prince of Air into Azeroth.",al={"who is demitrian","highlord demitrian thunderaan","how to summon thunderaan"}},{q="What happens when Thunderaan is summoned in Silithus?",a="Demitrian performs a dangerous ritual with the recovered bindings. What emerges becomes clear when the ritual is complete.",al={"thunderaan fight","what happens after summoning"},sp=1},{q="What weapon is tied to Thunderaan?",a="Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker, is the legendary sword tied to the Prince of Air. Demitrian's ritual reveals its fate.",al={"thunderfury","windseeker sword","thunderaan sword"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know Thunderaan as a pure and wrathful embodiment of air and lightning, and a spiritual custodian of the elements.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you seek the legend of Thunderfury, the storm-infused sword associated with the Prince of Air.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you covet the Prince of Air's fallen essence, bound within Thunderfury, for its unmatched speed and lightning-quick combat."},kw={"bindings","demitrian","garr","geddon","molten core","prince of air","ragnaros","silithus","thunderaan","thunderfury","windseeker"},rel={"npc:highlord-demitrian","zone:silithus","subzone:blackrock-mountain","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:skywall"},src={"Thunderaan"}}
E["subzone:bones-of-grakkarond"] = {t="subzone",n="Bones of Grakkarond",z="silithus",s="Across central Silithus, Grakkarond's bones lie beneath the sun. The bronze dragon fell in the ancient War of the Shifting Sands, and the Anubisath keep his remains sacred.",h="Across central Silithus, Grakkarond's bones lie beneath the sun.",sec={{t="A Monument of the Shifting Sands",b="Grakkarond's skull and ribcage lie across the dunes of central Silithus. A thousand years ago, he fell in the War of the Shifting Sands. In that great clash, Ossirian the Unscarred struck him down. Ossirian was an Anubisath warrior, empowered by the dark powers of the city-kingdom. The Anubisath leave the bones where Grakkarond fell, a sacred mark of their might against the dragonflights.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Whose bones are these?",a="These are the bones of Grakkarond, a great bronze dragon of the Bronze Dragonflight. A thousand years ago, he fell against the insectoid forces of Ahn'Qiraj in the War of the Shifting Sands.",al={"who was grakkarond","what dragon died here","dragon skeleton silithus"}},{q="Who killed Grakkarond?",a="Ossirian the Unscarred slew Grakkarond. An Anubisath warrior, he won great renown and dark blessings from Ahn'Qiraj's masters for his victory over the bronze wyrm.",al={"who killed the dragon","how did grakkarond die"}},{q="Why do the Anubisath revere this place?",a="The Anubisath revere the skeleton as a reminder of their decisive victory over a mighty dragonflight. It marks their strength against those who came to seal them away.",al={"why are the bones sacred","anubisath bones"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you can look to these bones and remember the War of the Shifting Sands. Your people and the four dragonflights fought side by side against the qiraji onslaught."},kw={"anubisath","bones of grakkarond","bronze dragon","grakkarond","ossirian the unscarred","silithus","war of the shifting sands"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Bones of Grakkarond"}}
E["subzone:bronzebeard-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Bronzebeard Encampment",z="silithus",s="In southern Silithus, Bronzebeard Encampment keeps a dwarven foothold east of the Scarab Wall. Explorer's League researchers study ancient silithid glyphs and mysteries buried beneath the desert.",h="In southern Silithus, Bronzebeard Encampment keeps a dwarven foothold east of the Scarab Wall.",sec={{t="A Foothold in the Shifting Sands",b="Bronzebeard Encampment stands near Silithus's southern bluffs, within sight of the Scarab Wall. Ironforge founded the camp for archaeological work. Researchers Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge study inscriptions and monuments left by forgotten civilizations. Scorching heat, scorpids, and silithid swarms make their work dangerous.",sp=0},{t="Glyphs and Desperation",b="At Bronzebeard Encampment, study goes hand in hand with survival. Silithid threats spread from underground hives, and the monstrous scorpid Deathclasp prowls nearby. Researchers rely on visiting adventurers to bring back rubbings of obscure glyphs, decipher ancient insectoid tongues, and find companions lost in the desert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Bronzebeard Encampment located?",a="Bronzebeard Encampment lies in southern Silithus, east of the Scarab Wall and north of the southern mountain ridge.",al={"where is bronzebeard encampment","bronzebeard camp location","how to find bronzebeard encampment"}},{q="Who runs the Bronzebeard Encampment?",a="Members and associates of the dwarven Explorer's League staff the camp. They include glyph researcher Rutgar Glyphshaper, Frankal Stonebridge, and their companion Glibb.",al={"who is at bronzebeard encampment","bronzebeard camp npcs","who leads bronzebeard camp"}},{q="What are the dwarves studying here?",a="The researchers study ancient stone glyphs, the silithid communication system, and long-buried secrets of southern Kalimdor.",al={"why are dwarves in silithus","what is rutgar studying","purpose of bronzebeard encampment"}},{q="What threats lurk near the encampment?",a="Aggressive silithid bugs, sand scorpions, and Deathclasp prowl the surrounding desert. Deathclasp is the giant scorpid known as Terror of the Sands, and nests just to the southeast.",al={"dangers near bronzebeard camp","deathclasp location","bronzebeard camp monsters"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see the Explorer's League's tenacity at work in this harsh desert. Ironforge researchers seek historical truth here.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Silithus, you can find a friendly camp far south of Cenarion Hold."},kw={"bronzebeard encampment","deathclasp","explorers league","frankal stonebridge","glibb","rutgar glyphshaper","scarab wall","silithus"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:scarab-wall","npc:rutgar-glyphshaper"},src={"Bronzebeard Encampment"}}
E["subzone:cenarion-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Cenarion Hold",z="silithus",s="Cenarion Hold watches over the ancient dangers beneath Silithus. The Cenarion Circle keeps its druids in this desert stronghold, guarding what lies buried under the sands.",h="Cenarion Hold watches over the ancient dangers beneath Silithus.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Dunes",b="In southern Silithus, Cenarion Hold directs the Cenarion Circle's work. You reach it by winding past Un'Goro Crater. Raised after the War of the Shifting Sands, the fortress watches over dormant threats sealed beneath the desert. Silithus is harsh country, home to silithid and arid storms. The hold gives shelter, trade, and supplies to night elf and tauren druids who keep watch over those buried dangers.",sp=0},{t="Neutral Ground",b="Cenarion Hold stays neutral because guarding the world from ancient evils matters beyond mortal quarrels. Alliance and Horde travelers may enter, and quartermasters and wardens welcome them despite precarious supply lines. Flight routes link the hold with outposts in Feralas, Tanaris, and Un'Goro Crater. It is the desert's only staging ground for adventurers investigating the unrest there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Cenarion Hold?",a="The Cenarion Circle governs and garrisons Cenarion Hold. Malfurion Stormrage founded the druidic order, and the neutral stronghold welcomes members of both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"who runs cenarion hold","cenarion hold faction","is cenarion hold neutral"}},{q="Why was the fortress built out here in the desert?",a="The fortress was built after the War of the Shifting Sands to watch over the ancient evil sealed deep beneath Silithus and suppress the silithid resurgence in the region.",al={"why is cenarion hold in silithus","purpose of cenarion hold","why did druids build here"}},{q="How do you travel to Cenarion Hold?",a="You can walk the steep mountain path northwest out of Un'Goro Crater. Flight routes link the hold to Gadgetzan, Un'Goro, and Feralas.",al={"how to get to cenarion hold","cenarion hold path","getting into silithus"}},{q="Can members of both factions use services here?",a="Yes. Merchants and flight handlers at Cenarion Hold serve any adventurer willing to brave the desert, whatever their allegiance.",al={"is it safe for horde","can alliance rest here","cenarion hold vendors"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find one of the largest druidic enclaves outside Moonglade at Cenarion Hold. It reflects the Circle's pledge to preserve natural balance against cosmic horrors.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Cenarion Hold as a tribute to the ancient sacrifices made during the War of the Shifting Sands millennia ago."},kw={"cenarion circle","cenarion hold","druids","kalimdor","shifting sands","silithid","silithus"},rel={"topic:cenarion-circle","zone:silithus","quest:5921","zone:ungoro","zone:feralas","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:old-god"},src={"Cenarion Hold"}}
E["subzone:crystal-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Crystal Vale",z="silithus",s="In northwestern Silithus, Crystal Vale gathers stone, wind, and ancient power. Jagged spires rise above rocky flats where earth and air elementals roam among rich ore veins. Potent summoning magic here is tied to the ancient elemental lords.",h="In northwestern Silithus, Crystal Vale gathers stone, wind, and ancient power.",sec={{t="A Confluence of Stone and Wind",b="Crystal Vale cuts a rocky basin into southern Silithus. Steep cliffs frame shimmering mineral formations, earthen elementals, and roaring whirlwinds of living air. Rich thorium draws a few prospectors, though the valley remains dangerous. Hostile elementals guard ground shaped by the primal conflicts of ancient Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="The Slumber of the Windseeker",b="Highlord Demitrian lingers in Crystal Vale with secrets about Prince Thunderaan, the Windseeker. Those who bring the fallen prince's severed elemental bindings and the rarest forged metals are directed to the valley. There, the imprisoned lord of air can be drawn from his bindings and faced in open battle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Crystal Vale located?",a="Crystal Vale lies in far northwestern Silithus, against the mountainous rim that borders the desert.",al={"where is crystal vale","crystal vale map","crystal vale location"}},{q="What creatures inhabit this valley?",a="Aggressive air and earth elementals roam among the valley's mineral outcrops.",al={"crystal vale mobs","what lives in crystal vale","elementals in crystal vale"}},{q="Who is Highlord Demitrian and why is he here?",a="Highlord Demitrian lives alone in Crystal Vale and knows much about Prince Thunderaan. He aids champions who can reunite the Windseeker's bindings and summon the elemental prince.",al={"who is demitrian","highlord demitrian crystal vale","demitrian location"}},{q="What is the Ravaged Twilight Camp?",a="Ravaged Twilight Camp is the wreckage of a Twilight's Hammer encampment in the valley. Violent elementals have shattered and overrun it.",al={"ravaged twilight camp crystal vale","twilight camp in vale","destroyed twilight camp"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Crystal Vale's craggy edges and canyon walls hold rich thorium veins. Mining can be lucrative there, but the valley is hazardous.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can witness the raw clash between earth and air spirits in Crystal Vale. It recalls the elementals' unrestrained chaos across Silithus."},kw={"crystal vale","elementals","highlord demitrian","ravaged twilight camp","silithus","thorium","thunderaan"},rel={"npc:highlord-demitrian","npc:thunderaan","subzone:ravaged-twilight-camp","zone:silithus"},src={"Crystal Vale"}}
E["subzone:hive-ashi"] = {t="subzone",n="Hive'Ashi",z="silithus",s="Across northern Silithus, Hive'Ashi sends its silithid swarms through sand and tunnel. It is one of three great hives in the region, with workers, defenders, and stingers moving over towering mounds.",h="Across northern Silithus, Hive'Ashi sends its silithid swarms through sand and tunnel.",sec={{t="The Northern Mound",b="In northern Silithus, Hive'Ashi's chitinous spires mark the ground claimed by a silithid swarm rising again. Workers forage while venomous defenders move south and east toward the Swarming Pillar. Beneath the mounds, dangerous tunnels shelter the colony. To learn what stirs in the desert, travelers must enter them.",sp=0},{t="A Threat Unearthed",b="Cenarion scouts keep watch on Hive'Ashi. They send combatants to thin the swarm and bring back reports from deep in the colony. Glyphs and coordinated behavior found in Ashi suggest the insects share a single will, though they seem mindless. Their numbers are swelling, and those guarding the southern borders make destroying the brood a priority before it spreads beyond northern Silithus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Hive'Ashi?",a="Hive'Ashi is an active silithid colony in northern Silithus. Thousands of burrowing insects hollow the desert into linked tunnels and mounds.",al={"ashi hive","hive ashi location","what is ashi"}},{q="What kinds of silithid live in Hive'Ashi?",a="Hive'Ashi shelters workers, sandstalkers, venomous stingers, and heavily armored defenders.",al={"ashi mobs","hive ashi creatures","what silithid are here"}},{q="How does Hive'Ashi relate to the Swarming Pillar?",a="Silithids spread outward from Hive'Ashi across the desert floor and swarm around the nearby Swarming Pillar.",al={"swarming pillar connection","ashi and swarming pillar"}},{q="Why are Cenarion scouts studying this hive?",a="The Cenarion Circle studies the silithid resurgence and how the hives coordinate. Scouts watch Ashi's strange glyphs and track how quickly the colony expands.",al={"why scout hive ashi","hive ashi scout report"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Cenarion Circle watches Silithus's corrupted sands. As a druid, you are called to study and suppress the insect menace pouring from Hive'Ashi before it engulfs the natural world.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance operative in Silithus, you help gather intelligence on Hive'Ashi so its aggressive swarms do not threaten neighboring lands across southern Kalimdor."},kw={"cenarion","hive ashi","hive'ashi","silithid","silithus","swarming pillar"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:swarming-pillar"},src={"Hive'Ashi"}}
E["subzone:hive-regal"] = {t="subzone",n="Hive'Regal",z="silithus",s="In southern Silithus, Hive'Regal's broods threaten the desert around one of its three great silithid colonies.",h="In southern Silithus, Hive'Regal's broods threaten the desert around one of its three great silithid colonies.",sec={{t="The Southern Hive",b="Hive'Regal spreads across southern Silithus, where silithid gather in great numbers. Resin spires rise above deep tunnels. Within them, dangerous broods range from venomous spitfires and burrowers to predatory slavemakers. The hive guards its borders and harvests organic material from travelers who stray too close.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Network",b="Beneath Silithus's red sands, Hive'Regal's passages reach deep into the earth. Strange glyphs mark the entrance and far places within the tunnels. They suggest an organized intelligence directs the swarm, beyond mere feral instinct. Scholars and scouts study Hive'Regal and its sister hives for signs of a greater power stirring beneath the wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Hive'Regal located?",a="Hive'Regal lies in southern Silithus, amid red sands and towering insectoid mounds.",al={"hive regal location","where is hive regal","find hive regal"}},{q="What kinds of creatures live in Hive'Regal?",a="Hostile silithid breeds live in Hive'Regal, including burrowers, ambushers, spitfires, and slavemakers that defend the hive.",al={"hive regal mobs","what is inside hive regal","hive regal enemies"}},{q="Why are researchers interested in Hive'Regal?",a="Scouts and scholars study Hive'Regal's strange wall glyphs to decipher them and monitor the silithid threat across southern Kalimdor.",al={"why go to hive regal","hive regal research","hive regal glyphs"}},{q="How does Hive'Regal differ from the other hives in Silithus?",a="Hive'Regal is the southernmost of Silithus's three major colonies, alongside Hive'Ashi and Hive'Zora. Each houses specialized silithid castes, and all appear to share a unified purpose.",al={"other hives silithus","three hives","difference between hives"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the Cenarion Circle watches Hive'Regal's spread closely. The Circle sees the invasive silithid corruption as an existential blight upon the desert ecosystem."},kw={"burrowers","hive","hive'regal","regal","silithid","silithus","slavemakers","spitfires"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Hive'Regal"}}
E["subzone:hive-zora"] = {t="subzone",n="Hive'Zora",z="silithus",s="Across western Silithus, Hive'Zora's silithid swarm spreads through the sands. It is one of three great hives in the desert, and its aggressive castes press outward.",h="Across western Silithus, Hive'Zora's silithid swarm spreads through the sands.",sec={{t="The Western Swarm",b="Stone spires rise from Hive'Zora's sands in western Silithus. Porous mounds mark entrances to deep tunnels carved by silithid burrowers. Waywatchers and reavers patrol the perimeter. Below, tunnelers and hive sisters brood. The Cenarion Circle and other scouts watch as the silithid menace presses into this ancient frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Hive'Zora?",a="Hive'Zora's surface spires lead into a vast network of tunnels beneath western Silithus.",al={"zora hive","what is hive zora","hive zora silithus"}},{q="What creatures live in Hive'Zora?",a="Silithid castes fill Hive'Zora. Waywatchers patrol outside, heavy reavers defend the ground, tunnelers excavate below, and venomous hive sisters dwell within.",al={"hive zora mobs","what monsters are in hive zora","who lives in hive zora"}},{q="Why is the Cenarion Circle investigating this hive?",a="Scouts and researchers in Silithus watch Hive'Zora to track the silithid threat's growth and movement. Envoys study silithid behavior, decipher their glyphs, and thin their growing numbers before the swarm overwhelms the region.",al={"why scout hive zora","cenarion circle hive zora"}},{q="How does Hive'Zora differ from the other hives in Silithus?",a="Hive'Zora lies farthest west among the three great hives. Hive'Ashi anchors the north, while Hive'Regal dominates the south. Each has its own brood, and all seek to spread across the desert.",al={"other hives silithus","difference between hives","hive regal hive ashi"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Druid of the Cenarion Circle, you see Hive'Zora's surge as unnatural, disrupting the desert wilds' natural balance.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you may find rich thorium veins and rare ooze-covered mineral deposits in the twisted tunnels and around silithid colonies like Hive'Zora."},kw={"cenarion circle","hive sisters","hive zora","hive'zora","reavers","silithid","silithus","waywatchers"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Hive'Zora"}}
E["subzone:ortell-s-hideout"] = {t="subzone",n="Ortell's Hideout",z="silithus",s="Hermit Ortell keeps to a cave against the mountains in southeastern Silithus. Few choose to live alone in this barren wasteland.",h="Hermit Ortell keeps to a cave against the mountains in southeastern Silithus.",sec={{t="A Hermit's Shelter",b="In southeastern Silithus, a cave among the cliffs shelters Hermit Ortell. Sandstorms sweep the wastes, and silithid swarms prowl beyond his door. He lives alone, far from civilization and the fortified garrisons of the Cenarion Hold. Travelers brave the dangerous route to this remote corner to seek his peculiar knowledge of the desert and its hazards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ortell's Hideout?",a="Ortell's Hideout lies in the mountain rock along Silithus's southeastern edge. It stands against the border cliffs, far from the central desert roads.",al={"where is ortell","ortell location","how to find ortell cave"}},{q="Who is Hermit Ortell?",a="Hermit Ortell lives alone in a small cave, apart from the Cenarion Circle expedition and the factions of the world. He chooses to dwell amid Silithus's dangers.",al={"who is ortell","hermit ortell lore"}},{q="Is Ortell's Hideout safe from the silithid?",a="The cave itself is free of silithid, but the surrounding zone is hostile, with silithid and Twilight's Hammer cultists. Reaching the hideout means crossing perilous terrain.",al={"are there bugs in the cave","is ortell cave safe"}}},kw={"cave","hermit ortell","ortell's hideout","silithus","southeastern silithus"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Ortell's Hideout"}}
E["subzone:ravaged-twilight-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Ravaged Twilight Camp",z="silithus",s="In the Crystal Vale of northwestern Silithus, Ravaged Twilight Camp lies broken and quiet. Highlord Demitrian remains there alone, devoted to the Windseeker.",h="In the Crystal Vale of northwestern Silithus, Ravaged Twilight Camp lies broken and quiet.",sec={{t="A Hermit's Ruin in the Vale",b="Twilight's Hammer keeps outposts across Silithus, yet its broken camp in the Crystal Vale is quiet and nearly deserted. Highlord Demitrian remains among the stones. He serves Thunderaan and broods over elemental bindings and the Windseeker's lost power, apart from the wider Twilight hierarchy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ravaged Twilight Camp?",a="Ravaged Twilight Camp lies in ruins in the Crystal Vale of northwestern Silithus. Highlord Demitrian makes his home there.",al={"ravaged twilight camp","ruined twilight camp silithus","crystal vale camp"}},{q="Who lives here?",a="Highlord Demitrian is the camp's sole notable resident. He is tied to elemental lore and the bindings of Prince Thunderaan.",al={"who is at the ravaged twilight camp","highlord demitrian location","camp npc"}},{q="Why is the camp ruined?",a="Cult records describe the camp as ruined. Highlord Demitrian remains among the wreckage, apart from Twilight's Hammer forces elsewhere in Silithus.",al={"why is it ravaged","what destroyed the camp","who attacked the camp"}},{q="Is the Twilight's Hammer hostile here?",a="No aggressive Twilight's Hammer patrols are in the camp. Unlike the camps across southern and central Silithus, it leaves Highlord Demitrian to brood in peace.",al={"are cultists attacking here","is demitrian hostile"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior seeking rumors of Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker, your path leads to Highlord Demitrian in this forsaken camp.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin seeking the legendary elemental armaments of antiquity, seek Demitrian in the Crystal Vale to unravel the vessel of Prince Thunderaan."},kw={"crystal vale","demitrian","highlord demitrian","ravaged twilight camp","silithus","thunderaan","thunderfury","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:crystal-vale","npc:highlord-demitrian","zone:silithus"},src={"Ravaged Twilight Camp"}}
E["subzone:scarab-dais"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarab Dais",z="silithus",s="Northwest of the Scarab Wall, the Scarab Dais holds the Scarab Gong in southern Silithus. The gong is tied to the wards that seal the qiraji within Ahn'Qiraj.",h="Northwest of the Scarab Wall, the Scarab Dais holds the Scarab Gong in southern Silithus.",sec={{t="The Gong of Ahn'Qiraj",b="Before the Scarab Wall, the Scarab Dais overlooks the sands where Ahn'Qiraj was sealed a millennium ago. The Scarab Gong rests on its stone platform, forged during the War of the Shifting Sands. Ancient night elven history and the bronze dragonflight say only the reconstructed Scepter of the Shifting Sands can break the magical barrier when it strikes the gong. Until then, horrors remain sealed beyond the wall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scarab Dais?",a="The Scarab Dais is a stone ceremonial terrace in southern Silithus, northwest of the Scarab Wall. It was built to house the Scarab Gong, which controls the magical wards sealing Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"what is this platform","scarab dais info","gong platform"}},{q="What happens if someone rings the gong on the dais?",a="Legend says striking the Scarab Gong with the restored Scepter of the Shifting Sands will shatter the wards across the Scarab Wall. The gates of Ahn'Qiraj will open, releasing the qiraji armies imprisoned within.",al={"what does the gong do","ring scarab gong","bang a gong"}},{q="Who watches over the Scarab Dais?",a="Jonathan the Revelator, a human Watcher of the bronze dragonflight and keeper of the Scarab Gong, watches over the gong and the sealed gate beyond from atop the dais.",al={"who is at the dais","bronze dragons at the dais","jonathan the revelator"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the Scarab Dais recalls the tragic War of the Shifting Sands a thousand years ago. Night elves and dragonflights paid in blood to seal the qiraji behind the wall."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","jonathan the revelator","scarab dais","scarab gong","scarab wall","shifting sands","silithus"},rel={"subzone:scarab-wall","zone:silithus"},src={"Scarab Dais"}}
E["subzone:scarab-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarab Wall",z="silithus",s="At Silithus's southern edge, the Scarab Wall bars the way to Ahn'Qiraj. Stone and bronze dragonflight sorcery keep the ancient swarms sealed beyond it, as they have since the War of the Shifting Sands.",h="At Silithus's southern edge, the Scarab Wall bars the way to Ahn'Qiraj.",sec={{t="Shield Against the Shadow",b="The Scarab Wall runs across the desert from east to west. It was raised a thousand years ago, after the War of the Shifting Sands. The qiraji nearly destroyed the night elf armies and their dragon allies before they drove the swarms back into their ancient kingdom.\n\nTo hold the qiraji there, the allies raised a great rampart of desert stone. The bronze dragonflight crowned it with a magical barrier. The wall cut the insectoid armies off from Kalimdor, yet their dread presence still hangs behind its stones.",sp=0},{t="A Sealed Ruin",b="Beyond the sandstone wall and its draconic wards lies Ahn'Qiraj, stronghold of the ancient qiraji. The wall was raised to imprison their armies after the War of the Shifting Sands. Its gates can be opened by ringing the Scarab Gong with the Scepter of the Shifting Sands, a relic tied to the dragons and Fandral Staghelm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Scarab Wall?",a="Stone and magic bar the southern edge of Silithus at the Scarab Wall. Beyond it lie Ahn'Qiraj and its ancient insectoid swarms, sealed in the desert ruins.",al={"scarab wall purpose","what is this wall in silithus","ahn qiraj wall"}},{q="Who built the Scarab Wall?",a="The night elves and bronze dragonflight raised the Scarab Wall together at the end of the War of the Shifting Sands. Stone sealed the qiraji inside, and the dragons wove a vast magical barrier above it.",al={"who made the wall","who created the scarab wall"}},{q="Why was the Scarab Wall raised?",a="The night elves and their dragon allies raised the Scarab Wall after driving the qiraji swarms back into Ahn'Qiraj. There they sealed them away, bringing the War of the Shifting Sands to an end.",al={"why was the scarab wall built","purpose of the scarab wall"}},{q="Can players go past the wall?",a="The Scarab Wall seals Ahn'Qiraj, but its gates can be opened by ringing the Scarab Gong with the Scepter of the Shifting Sands.",al={"can you go past scarab wall","how to get past wall in silithus"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the Scarab Wall recalls the terrible sacrifices of the War of the Shifting Sands, when an entire generation was lost to halt the swarm.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you feel life unnaturally suppressed around the wall. Ancient wards struggle to contain a corruptive blight beneath the earth."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","bronze dragonflight","qiraji","scarab wall","silithus","war of the shifting sands"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:old-god","subzone:valor-s-rest"},src={"Scarab Wall"}}
E["subzone:southwind-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Southwind Village",z="silithus",s="In Southwind Village, fallen defenders haunt the ruins beneath Silithus’s sands. The qiraji destroyed the night elf outpost during the War of the Shifting Sands, and silithid still prowl the dunes.",h="In Southwind Village, fallen defenders haunt the ruins beneath Silithus’s sands.",sec={{t="A Tragedy in the Sands",b="During the War of the Shifting Sands, a thousand years ago, Southwind Village held a night elf stronghold. When qiraji legions broke through its defenses, Valstann Staghelm led a detachment to hold the village. He was the son of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm. The defenders were overwhelmed and slaughtered, and General Rajaxx dragged Valstann away into captivity. The village lay in ruins, its buildings fractured beneath the sun.",sp=0},{t="The Tormented Dead",b="A thousand years after the fall, Southwind Village still bears the marks of the assault. The slain night elf Sentinels and druids could not move on. Driven mad by the horror of their final moments, their spirits roam the crumbled stone walls without end, led by the Shade of Ambermoon. They lash out at anyone who enters, while predatory silithid swarm across the surrounding dunes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to Southwind Village?",a="The qiraji destroyed Southwind Village during the War of the Shifting Sands a thousand years ago. Their army overwhelmed the night elf garrison, slaughtered its defenders, and ruined the outpost.",al={"why is southwind ruined","southwind lore","what destroyed southwind village"}},{q="Who was Valstann Staghelm?",a="Valstann Staghelm was the beloved son of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm. He led Southwind Village’s defense against the invading qiraji, but his troops were overwhelmed and General Rajaxx dragged him away into captivity.",al={"valstann staghelm southwind","fandral staghelm son","who defended southwind"}},{q="Why are there night elf ghosts here?",a="The brutal slaughter trapped the spirits of Southwind Village’s slain druids and Sentinels in the ruins. They remain caught in an endless loop of their final battle, with the Shade of Ambermoon among them.",al={"southwind spirits","why are there ghosts in southwind","shade of ambermoon"}},{q="Are the bugs related to what destroyed the village?",a="Yes. Silithid swarm around the ruins as part of the wider insectoid force tied to the qiraji, who invaded Silithus and destroyed the outpost.",al={"silithid southwind","are bugs connected to southwind"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Southwind Village as one of your people’s most painful defeats. Its tortured specters are fellow kaldorei, still awaiting peace.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the ruined grove-like structures and tormented spirits of ancient druids in Southwind. They recall nature’s loss against the insectoid hordes."},kw={"fandral staghelm","qiraji","rajaxx","shade of ambermoon","silithus","southwind village","valstann staghelm","war of the shifting sands"},rel={"zone:silithus","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:night-elf","topic:sentinels","topic:druid"},src={"Southwind Village"}}
E["subzone:staghelm-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Staghelm Point",z="silithus",s="In northeastern Silithus, Staghelm Point keeps watch over the desert and Twilight's Run. Its ancient night elf tower looks over encroaching dunes, while old threats linger in nearby caverns.",h="In northeastern Silithus, Staghelm Point keeps watch over the desert and Twilight's Run.",sec={{t="A Silent Watch Above the Sands",b="Staghelm Point rises above the dry flats of northeastern Silithus. A lone night elf tower keeps watch over the wasteland, with cultists in nearby caves such as Twilight's Run. Ralo'shan the Eternal Watcher guards the outpost, and a bronze drake circles overhead. The tower bears the Staghelm name, recalling the great sacrifices the Kaldorei made during the ancient War of the Shifting Sands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Staghelm Point?",a="Ralo'shan the Eternal Watcher guards the tower. A bronze drake from the Brood of Nozdormu patrols the skies above.",al={"who is at staghelm point","staghelm point npcs","raloshan"}},{q="What threats lie nearby?",a="Twilight's Run lies down the path from the peak. The cavern and its surrounding camp hold fanatical members of the Twilight's Hammer cult.",al={"staghelm point danger","nearby enemies","twilights run"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can remember the sacrifices the Kaldorei made during the War of the Shifting Sands to hold back the horrors beneath Silithus.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can look across Silithus's dry, corrupted wilderness from the tower bearing the Staghelm name. Nature's balance has been broken there."},kw={"bronze drake","fandral staghelm","ralo'shan","silithus","staghelm point","twilight's run","watchtower"},rel={"zone:silithus","npc:fandral-staghelm","subzone:twilight-s-run","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:night-elf"},src={"Staghelm Point"}}
E["subzone:swarming-pillar"] = {t="subzone",n="Swarming Pillar",z="silithus",s="Winged silithid circle Swarming Pillar, south of Cenarion Hold. Their swarm has carved and reshaped the rock into a hive in central Silithus.",h="Winged silithid circle Swarming Pillar, south of Cenarion Hold.",sec={{t="A Spire of Chitin and Sand",b="In central Silithus, Swarming Pillar rises from the dunes, its natural rock carved into burrows and coated with the swarm’s resin. It lies just south of Cenarion Hold. From it, winged worker and soldier broods pour out in dark clouds that fill the desert air and warn travelers away.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Hive",b="Swarming Pillar is only the visible tip of a vast underground network. Deep tunnels and cavernous breeding chambers beneath its stony exterior anchor one of the region’s largest hives. The Cenarion Circle watches with concern as active broods threaten its druidic operations and expose the coordination behind the silithid menace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Swarming Pillar?",a="Swarming Pillar is a rock formation in central Silithus, overtaken and reshaped into an active silithid hive. Flying insectoids circle its peak in an endless swarm.",al={"swarming pillar","what is this pillar","silithid spire silithus"}},{q="Where is the Swarming Pillar located?",a="Swarming Pillar rises in the desert’s center, just south of Cenarion Hold.",al={"where is swarming pillar","swarming pillar location"}},{q="Why are there so many bugs flying around it?",a="Swarming Pillar houses one of Silithus’s primary hives, a massive nursery and transit point for winged silithid that patrol the surrounding sands.",al={"why swarming","flying bugs silithus pillar","flying silithid"}},{q="Is the Swarming Pillar connected to the hives beneath the sand?",a="Yes. The visible spire is the uppermost projection of an extensive colony, with tunnels carved deep into the bedrock and sands beneath Silithus.",al={"hive tunnels","underground silithid pillar"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the hive at Swarming Pillar as an affront to the natural order. So close to Cenarion Hold, it remains a danger to the Cenarion Circle’s watch."},kw={"cenarion hold","hive","insects","silithid","silithus","spire","swarming pillar"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:cenarion-hold"},src={"Swarming Pillar"}}
E["subzone:twilight-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Base Camp",z="silithus",s="At Twilight Base Camp, the Twilight's Hammer gathers in Silithus to summon elemental powers and advance its apocalyptic cause. Wind stones mark the camp, and armed cultists stand ready.",h="At Twilight Base Camp, the Twilight's Hammer gathers in Silithus to summon elemental powers and advance its...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Doom",b="Twilight Base Camp is one of several Twilight's Hammer enclaves in Silithus. Zealots, geomancers, and stonecallers gather among jagged ritual stones to summon elemental forces. Twilight Keeper Havunth and Twilight Lord Everun direct their efforts to hasten Azeroth's end. Cenarion Hold forces seek to restore balance to the region, but the cult openly defies them.",sp=0},{t="The Wind Stones",b="Lesser and greater wind stones stand throughout the outpost. The Twilight's Hammer uses cryptic incantations and cult regalia at these monuments to draw chaotic elemental spirits into the physical realm. Travelers and scouts work to disrupt the rites before the cult's influence spreads across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Twilight Base Camp?",a="Twilight Base Camp is an armed Twilight's Hammer outpost in the Silithus deserts. Cultists conduct rituals there to summon elemental entities.",al={"twilight camp silithus","what is twilight base camp","silithus cultist camp"}},{q="Who controls this camp?",a="Zealots of the Twilight's Hammer man the outpost under overseers such as Twilight Keeper Havunth and Twilight Lord Everun.",al={"who leads twilight base camp","twilight base camp leader","who is in charge"}},{q="What are the strange stones in the camp?",a="The wind stones are mystical conduits of varying size. Cultists use them to pierce planar barriers and bind elemental creatures to their service.",al={"wind stones","lesser wind stone","greater wind stone silithus"}},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer in Silithus?",a="The Twilight's Hammer seeks the chaotic energies beneath Silithus's sands. They hope to awaken dark powers and summon elementals to destroy the world.",al={"why twilight hammer silithus","twilight cult silithus goal"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see the cult's use of wind stones to subjugate elemental spirits as an affront to spiritual harmony.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face the threat the cult's apocalyptic rites pose to peace. The Holy Light calls you to answer."},kw={"silithus","twilight avenger","twilight base camp","twilight geolord","twilight keeper havunth","twilight lord everun","twilight's hammer","wind stones"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Twilight Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:twilight-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Outpost",z="silithus",s="At Twilight Outpost, the Twilight's Hammer gathers in southwestern Silithus. Its Wind Stones summon elemental horrors near the Scarab Wall.",h="At Twilight Outpost, the Twilight's Hammer gathers in southwestern Silithus.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Whispers",b="In southwestern Silithus, Twilight Outpost is one of the Twilight's Hammer's great strongholds. You find it northwest of the Scarab Wall and west of the Bronzebeard Encampment. Twilight Avengers, Geolords, and Stonecallers fill the camp. Twilight Keeper Exeter and the rare Twilight Lord Everun lead these zealots in service to their apocalyptic masters.",sp=0},{t="The Wind Stones",b="Wind Stones stand scattered through the camp, from Lesser to Greater. The Twilight's Hammer uses enchanted regalia and foul incantations to tear open paths to the elemental planes. Abyssal commanders and elemental lords emerge through those breaches. Disrupting the summons is one way to strike back at the cult's hold in the desert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Outpost located?",a="Twilight Outpost lies in southwestern Silithus, northwest of the Scarab Wall and west of the Bronzebeard Encampment.",al={"twilight outpost location","where is twilight outpost","find twilight outpost"}},{q="Who occupies the Twilight Outpost?",a="The Twilight's Hammer occupies the encampment. Its ranks include Twilight Avengers, Geolords, Stonecallers, and Twilight Masters, led by figures such as Twilight Keeper Exeter and Twilight Lord Everun.",al={"who is at twilight outpost","twilight outpost enemies","cultists in silithus"}},{q="What are the Wind Stones found in the camp?",a="Wind Stones range from Lesser to Greater and let the cult breach the elemental planes. Cultists channel dark energies through them to summon elemental lords and Abyssal commanders into Azeroth.",al={"what are wind stones","greater wind stone silithus","lesser wind stone silithus"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer gathered near the Scarab Wall?",a="The Twilight's Hammer gathers near the Scarab Wall for the ancient dark energies beneath Silithus. The cult establishes camps there to summon elementals and harness chaotic forces stirring beyond the sealed gates.",al={"why are cultists in silithus","twilight hammer purpose silithus"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you stand against the Twilight's Hammer's corruption and its command of elemental spirits through Wind Stones. That command defies the elements' natural balance.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face the Twilight's Hammer's nihilistic zealotry as an affront to the Light. Bring holy wrath against its foul summonings in the desert."},kw={"bronzebeard encampment","scarab wall","silithus","twilight keeper exeter","twilight lord everun","twilight outpost","twilight's hammer","wind stone"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer","subzone:scarab-wall","subzone:bronzebeard-encampment"},src={"Twilight Outpost"}}
E["subzone:twilight-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Post",z="silithus",s="Twilight Post holds the Twilight's Hammer in a fortified camp in northwestern Silithus. Far west of Cenarion Hold and northwest of Twilight Base Camp, its cultists use wind stones to contact otherworldly forces. Adventurers here face zealous defenders and the stones that serve their rites.",h="Twilight Post holds the Twilight's Hammer in a fortified camp in northwestern Silithus.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Elemental Zealotry",b="Twilight Post is a fortified outpost in northwestern Silithus. Heavily armed defenders and ritualists fill the camp, among them Twilight Avengers, Geolords, and Stonecallers. Twilight Keeper Mayna leads them, with the rare fanatic Twilight Lord Everun at her side.\n\nAt the heart of the post stand Lesser, regular, and Greater Wind Stones. Through dark rites and communion with the elements, the cultists use them to call elemental horrors from realms beyond and bind them. Such rites threaten the fragile peace the Cenarion Circle keeps in the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Twilight Post located?",a="Twilight Post stands in far northwestern Silithus, well west of Cenarion Hold and northwest of the larger Twilight Base Camp.",al={"twilight post location","where is twilight post","twilight post silithus map"}},{q="Who occupies the Twilight Post?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult occupies Twilight Post. Twilight Keeper Mayna and Twilight Lord Everun are stationed there, guarded by ranks of Twilight Avengers, Geolords, and Stonecallers.",al={"who is at twilight post","twilight post mobs","enemies at twilight post"}},{q="What are the wind stones found in the camp?",a="The Lesser, regular, and Greater Wind Stones are arcane conduits. The Twilight's Hammer uses them to summon and bind elemental creatures to its service.",al={"what are wind stones","wind stones silithus","lesser wind stone twilight post"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer operating in Silithus?",a="The Twilight's Hammer has flocked to Silithus to awaken and commune with ancient, dark powers beneath the sands. Its elemental summonings also bolster the cult's ranks.",al={"why are cultists in silithus","twilight hammer silithus goal"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the Twilight's Hammer twists the sacred communion of the elements. At outposts like this, its cultists use wind stones to summon and bind spirits by force.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the Cenarion Circle watches the cult's outposts closely. Its dark elemental rites threaten Silithus's fragile, scarred balance."},kw={"geolord","silithus","stonecaller","twilight keeper mayna","twilight lord everun","twilight post","twilight's hammer","wind stone"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:twilight-base-camp","subzone:cenarion-hold"},src={"Twilight Post"}}
E["subzone:twilight-s-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight's Run",z="silithus",s="Beneath Staghelm Point in northern Silithus, Twilight's Run shelters the Twilight's Hammer. Its cavern walls shield their rituals and forces from the desert winds.",h="Beneath Staghelm Point in northern Silithus, Twilight's Run shelters the Twilight's Hammer.",sec={{t="A Subterranean Redoubt",b="Beneath Staghelm Point, Twilight's Run opens into the northern cliffs of Silithus. The Twilight's Hammer has made its tunnels a stronghold, sheltered from desert winds and the silithid hives that roam the dunes. Its cultists gather to commune with dark forces, guard ritual materials, and marshal their forces.\n\nVyral the Vile and other overseers direct the cultists. They keep a hostile watch and stand ready to strike down any traveler or scout who comes too close.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Twilight's Run located?",a="Twilight's Run lies in the northern mountains of Silithus, beneath Staghelm Point.",al={"where is twilights run","twilights run location","how to find twilights run"}},{q="Who occupies Twilight's Run?",a="The Twilight's Hammer occupies Twilight's Run. Among them are Vyral the Vile, Twilight Overlords, and Twilight Flamereavers.",al={"who is inside twilights run","twilights run mobs","who lives in twilights run"}},{q="What is the cult doing inside the cavern?",a="The Twilight's Hammer uses Twilight's Run as a sheltered outpost. There, the cult keeps out of the desert winds while pursuing its apocalyptic work.",al={"twilight cult purpose silithus cave","why are cultists in twilights run"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may find the zealous nihilists in Twilight's Run an affront to the holy tenets of the Light. They serve dark powers."},kw={"silithus","staghelm point","twilight cult","twilight's hammer","twilight's run","twilights run","vyral the vile"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer","subzone:staghelm-point"},src={"Twilight's Run"}}
E["subzone:valor-s-rest"] = {t="subzone",n="Valor's Rest",z="silithus",s="At Silithus's eastern edge, Valor's Rest gives travelers shelter beside its cemetery.",h="At Silithus's eastern edge, Valor's Rest gives travelers shelter beside its cemetery.",sec={{t="Gateway to the Dunes",b="At Silithus's eastern border, Valor's Rest stands beside the ramp down from Un'Goro Crater. The Cenarion Circle keeps the camp neutral. Alliance and Horde travelers gather there before crossing into the arid wastes. Its graveyard marks those lost to the desert, where insectoid horrors and ancient threats endanger even the hardiest travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Valor's Rest located?",a="Valor's Rest lies at Silithus's eastern entrance, along the path from Un'Goro Crater's northwestern corner into the desert.",al={"valors rest location","how to find valors rest","where is valors rest"}},{q="Who controls Valor's Rest?",a="The Cenarion Circle keeps Valor's Rest neutral for Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"who runs valors rest","valors rest faction","cenarion circle camp silithus"}},{q="What is the notable feature of this camp?",a="Valor's Rest is known for its graveyard, where those claimed by the desert and its insectoid inhabitants are buried.",al={"valors rest graveyard","what is at valors rest"}},{q="Is Valor's Rest safe from the surrounding wildlife?",a="Insect infestations reach the area around Valor's Rest, warning of the swarm deeper in Silithus.",al={"valors rest safe","is valors rest under attack"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the Cenarion Circle keeping watch at Valor's Rest as troubling stirrings trouble the southern desert.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find a small refuge at Valor's Rest after emerging from Un'Goro's wilds. The Horde shares it under Cenarion neutrality."},kw={"camp","cenarion circle","graveyard","silithus","un'goro crater","valor's rest"},rel={"zone:silithus","zone:ungoro","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Valor's Rest"}}
E["zone:silithus"] = {t="zone",n="Silithus",z="silithus",s="Silithus lies beneath spreading silithid swarms, watched by the Cenarion Circle. The desert holds the ancient ruins of Ahn'Qiraj, sealed behind the Scarab Wall a thousand years ago. Druids guard against the swarms and Twilight's Hammer cultists.",h="Silithus lies beneath spreading silithid swarms, watched by the Cenarion Circle.",sec={{t="The Desert Frontier",b="You enter Silithus from Un'Goro Crater through a broad, rocky pass in its northwest corner. Jungle gives way to dunes, jagged stone, and towering hives. Water is scarce, and the wind carries the hum of insect wings across the sand. Near the desert's center, Cenarion Hold offers shelter to travelers, researchers, and warriors. The Cenarion Circle keeps this outpost as the only refuge in the hostile wastes.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Shifting Sands",b="A thousand years ago, night elves and the great dragonflights fought desperately to drive back the Qiraji in the War of the Shifting Sands. The Qiraji were an insectoid empire born from the ancient Aqiri civilization.\n\nWhen victory proved beyond reach, the defenders sealed the swarms inside their stronghold with the Scarab Wall and enchanted Scarab Dais. The gates held, but silithids burrowed through tunnels below and formed vast colonies across the desert, including Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal.",sp=0},{t="A Converging Storm",b="Twilight's Hammer has fortified several outposts in Silithus. Its cultists summon elemental terrors and worship the dark power beneath Ahn'Qiraj. Cenarion Circle observers watch the silithid colonies spread and keep guard against the ancient threat behind the Scarab Wall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Silithus on foot?",a="Travel through Un'Goro Crater to its northwestern corner. Near a bend in the serpentine river, a sloping dirt road climbs between two prominent stone pillars and passes through the crater wall into Silithus.",al={"silithus entrance","how to get to silithus","silithus path"}},{q="What is the Scarab Wall?",a="The Scarab Wall is a massive enchanted barrier in southern Silithus. A thousand years ago, night elves and the dragonflights raised it during the War of the Shifting Sands to imprison the Qiraji empire within Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"ahn'qiraj gate","scarab wall","the big wall in silithus"}},{q="Who runs Cenarion Hold?",a="The Cenarion Circle established and runs Cenarion Hold. Its druids and allied guardians watch the silithid swarms, investigate ancient ruins, and welcome neutral travelers from both the Alliance and Horde.",al={"who is in cenarion hold","cenarion hold faction","cenarion hold friendly"}},{q="What are the giant insect mounds across the zone?",a="The giant mounds are the silithids' great underground hives: Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal. Each holds a sprawling tunnel network and distinct insectoid castes that serve the wills locked behind Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"silithus hives","bug hives silithus","hive ashi hive zora"}},{q="What is the Twilight's Hammer doing here?",a="Twilight's Hammer maintains several fortified bases in Silithus, including Twilight Base Camp and Twilight Post. Its cultists perform foul rites to summon elementals and worship the ancient, malevolent entities entombed behind the Scarab Wall.",al={"twilight cultists silithus","twilight outpost silithus","why is twilight's hammer in silithus"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are called to Silithus, where the Cenarion Circle keeps its southern Kalimdor operations. Help stem the land's corruption and face the unnatural broods threatening nature's balance.",["profession:Mining"]="Silithus's dry rocks and insect tunnels hold some of the world's richest Thorium deposits. Rare ooze-covered veins lie hidden within the silithid hives.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Rare plants flourish despite Silithus's harsh desert: Mountain Silversage, Dreamfoil, Sungrass, and the prized Black Lotus.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you walk the grim ground where your ancestors bled in the War of the Shifting Sands. Thousands sacrificed their lives to seal Ahn'Qiraj's gates."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","cenarion hold","hive'ashi","hive'regal","hive'zora","scarab dais","scarab wall","silithid","silithus","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:cenarion-hold","subzone:scarab-wall","subzone:scarab-dais","zone:ungoro","subzone:hive-ashi","subzone:hive-zora","subzone:hive-regal","topic:cenarion-circle"},src={"Silithus (Classic)","Silithus"}}
